From 760b0d5347cbf266a57cc000c6fb0b2782d5c176 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 19:44:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] fixup! gluon-mesh-batman-adv: detect
 throughput_override for tunnel hardifs

tunnel_hardifs() applied the WAN uplink speed to every batadv hardif
without a native sysfs speed. That is correct for mesh-vpn and the
mesh-on-WAN hardif vx_mesh_uplink (both ride the uplink), but wrong for
vx_mesh_other, the mesh-on-LAN hardif that rides a dedicated wired mesh
port: its throughput is the local link speed, so tagging it with the
uplink speed misreports batman-V's routing metric.

Keep all the VXLAN hardifs (an override still beats batman-V's 1 Mbit/s
default) but choose the speed source per hardif: vx_mesh_other takes the
min carrier-up speed of the role=mesh (non-uplink) ports via the new
mesh_other_speed_kbit(); mesh-vpn and vx_mesh_uplink keep the uplink
speed. The shared carrier/speed walk is factored into
min_link_speed_kbit().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
